1
00:00:00,553 --> 00:00:02,553
(Sheldon:)That's because
I'm not being challenged.

2
00:00:02,763 --> 00:00:04,723
(Sheldon:)It's the same reason
Einstein failed math.

3
00:00:04,932 --> 00:00:07,062
(Amy:)Maybe the math
was too bubbly for him.

4
00:00:07,602 --> 00:00:10,232
(Sheldon:)You think you're doing science
by cutting up that brain?

5
00:00:10,438 --> 00:00:12,108
They could do the same at Quiznos.

6
00:00:12,315 --> 00:00:15,565
(Sheldon:)And they'd offer to toast it for me too.

7
00:00:16,736 --> 00:00:17,986
(Amy:)Okay, smart guy.

8
00:00:18,195 --> 00:00:22,155
(Amy:)I'm about to remove the locus coeruleus,
which is incredibly delicate work.

9
00:00:22,783 --> 00:00:24,413
(Amy:)Have at it.

10
00:00:25,703 --> 00:00:27,373
(Amy:)All right.

11
00:00:28,205 --> 00:00:31,295
(Sheldon:)I'm no stranger to a little gray matter.

12
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:41,510
(Amy:)Locus coeruleus.

13
00:00:41,719 --> 00:00:44,889
(Amy:)You're getting warmer.
It is indeed in the brain.

14
00:00:46,766 --> 00:00:49,606
(Amy:)Hope your hands are steady.
It's the width of a single hair.

15
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:53,060
(Amy:)But this is just biology,
so it's no problem for a genius like you.

16
00:00:53,272 --> 00:00:56,362
It's not. I will have you know
in the field of physics we work...

17
00:00:56,567 --> 00:01:02,027
(Sheldon:)...with particles so small they make
fat jokes about the locus coeruleus...

